        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Dukey has this *unwritten rule* that we didn\u2019t agree to, but apparently we all live by now:\n\n\ud83d\udc49 if he can reach us\u2026 he *must* be touching us.\n\nNot cuddling. Not sitting next to us. No no. Just one single paw\u2026 placed very intentionally like he\u2019s clocking in for his shift.\n\nOn our leg? Paw.  \nOn our hand? Paw.  \nOn our shoulder while we\u2019re minding our business? Paw.  \nTrying to work? Congrats, now he\u2019s HR and we\u2019re all under supervision.\n\nHe doesn\u2019t want attention. He doesn\u2019t want pets. He just needs to *know* we\u2019re there\u2026 at all times\u2026 like a tiny, furry emotional support ankle monitor.\n\nHonestly at this point we don\u2019t even question it anymore. If he\u2019s not touching one of us, we start wondering what\u2019s wrong \ud83d\ude05\n\nAnyone else have a cat that believes in \u2728mandatory contact\u2728 or is Dukey just built different?"
          ]
        },
        "create_time": 1776187840.242365,
        "id": "ae7b6734-2082-4d43-9c67-17437887b0fd",
